prompts.template:
Here is a chapter called "{title}".

{role:text}

Where would a reader put this down? Be specific about paragraphs. Name what is limp, what is explained twice, and what the chapter is avoiding. Do not rewrite it.

The outline for "{title}":

{role:outline}

The chapter as written:

{role:text}

What did the chapter promise and not deliver? What did it do that the outline did not account for? Say whether the drift is an improvement or a problem.

A chapter called "{title}":

{role:text}

Quote three lines of dialogue and say who could have said them. If any of them could belong to anyone, say so plainly — that is the problem to fix.

This chapter ends where you can see:

{role:text}

Suggest three ways the next chapter could open that do not simply continue the scene. One sentence each, no explanation.
